    "note": "**GATE 4, TAKE 2 — ring rebuilt on current conventions** (forked from candidate-01, rejected: sliver-seam squares + weak animation).\n\nThe white squares WERE the construction: the premium sweep bbox-snapped ~N slivers to a coarse grid, and the rectangular snap corners printed at the segment gaps on every frame. That machinery existed only to keep mask counts under the overlay cliff for the draw-on.\n\n**Rebuild:** ONE construction for every mode — a full-cell inline-mask per segment (seam-free by construction, the same clean masks the static ring always used). Premium = clockwise staggered alpha BLOOM: each segment starts as the eased front reaches its start angle and fades over a duration proportional to its own arc, so the reveal advances like a continuous clockwise build. Light = same stagger as enable pops. The whole sliver apparatus (placePiece, letterbox, 96-division quantize, overlap constants) is DELETED — ~90 fewer lines, ≤MAX_SEGMENTS masks in every mode.\n\nEverything from candidate-01 still holds: content-hug legend + width-caps, equal-band legend stack, debugLayout contract (legend-swatch equal 2%+1px). 53/53 unit (sweep tests → bloom tests), e2e 7/7, battery ×14 canvases ×5 configs.\n\nStill open from take 1: the legend LOOK-SHIFT call, cover?, tutorial?, and the portrait `legend: bottom` design question.",
